{:edb/db-before-t 1972 :edb/db-after-t 1973 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535285 50 #inst "2026-10-08T21:14:07.064Z" 13194139535285 true] [17592186064079 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341669 13194139535285 true] [17592186064079 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341683 13194139535285 true] [17592186064080 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341676 13194139535285 true] [17592186064080 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341690 13194139535285 true] [17592186064080 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341693 13194139535285 true] [17592186341669 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341670 13194139535285 true] [17592186341669 1089 "q-20976" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341669 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535285 true] [17592186341669 1100 "For the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-24x+5,$ defined on the closed interval $-2\\le x\\le 2,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The global maximum value is $45$\n- The global minimum value is $-14$\n- The global maximum value is $18$" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341669 1113 #uuid "302cb8da-ded5-5011-8c1e-b60b334aa94d" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341669 1145 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-24x+5,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x-24,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x-24 & =0 \\\\ 12({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x-2) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x-2 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+2)-(x+2) & =0 \\\\ (x+2)({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-1)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,-1,\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=-2,\\,-1,\\,1,$ and the endpoints $x=-2,2$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =3(-2)^{4}+8(-2)^{3}-6(-2)^{2}-24(-2)+5=13 \\\\ f(-1) & =3(-1)^{4}+8(-1)^{3}-6(-1)^{2}-24(-1)+5=18 \\\\ f(1) & =3(1)^{4}+8(1)^{3}-6(1)^{2}-24(1)+5=-14 \\\\ f(2) & =3(2)^{4}+8(2)^{3}-6(2)^{2}-24(2)+5=45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(2)=45,$ so the global maximum is $45.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(1)=-14,$ so the global minimum is $-14.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/9b48417439d0e018250328b92561732dd9f4c8bbec157daf33287b20dac7c41f.png)" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341671 13194139535285 true] [17592186341670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341672 13194139535285 true] [17592186341670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341673 13194139535285 true] [17592186341670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341674 13194139535285 true] [17592186341670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341675 13194139535285 true] [17592186341670 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535285 true] [17592186341670 1041 "selection" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341670 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341674 13194139535285 true] [17592186341670 1110 #uuid "d6d66fdf-bbb7-5d6e-b93c-ae1dcaac0321" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341671 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341671 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535285 true] [17592186341671 1111 #uuid "e0c7c6d9-551c-5844-83f9-f3e199afc52f" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341672 1034 "I only" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341672 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535285 true] [17592186341672 1111 #uuid "7aba49aa-8dab-5788-b79e-9e9783b4b204" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341673 1034 "III only" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341673 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535285 true] [17592186341673 1111 #uuid "4f46b4eb-16b2-5b9e-a3de-404f078480e6" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341674 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341674 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535285 true] [17592186341674 1111 #uuid "271a81cd-eaa3-5ec9-93e1-61a648e3a523" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341675 1034 "II only" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341675 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535285 true] [17592186341675 1111 #uuid "a5ad553c-d7b9-5104-9e02-fc5b565fbd8c" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341676 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341677 13194139535285 true] [17592186341676 1089 "q-2689" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341676 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535285 true] [17592186341676 1100 "Find the global minimum value of the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{2}$ on the closed interval $-3\\le x\\le 1.$" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341676 1113 #uuid "b6187976-1be0-519f-b378-82888b36e23d" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341676 1145 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3}-16x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-16x & =0 \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ 4x(x-2)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,0,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-3,1]$, the critical points are $x=-2,0,$ and the endpoints $x=-3,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =(-3)^{4}-8(-3)^{2}=9 \\\\ f(-2) & =(-2)^{4}-8(-2)^{2}=-16 \\\\ f(0) & =(0)^{4}-8(0)^{2}=0 \\\\ f(1) & =(1)^{4}-8(1)^{2}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-3)=9,$ so the global maximum is $9.$\n\n- The least value is $f(-2)=-16,$ so the global minimum is $-16.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061690/assets/e57ff9bc04fb9d9db592dda6aac9c364fd5f2e6fcd52968627b1e0271919f5bb.png)" 13194139535285 true] [17592186341677 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341678 13194139535285 true] [17592186341677 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341679 13194139535285 true] [17592186341677 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341680 13194139535285 true] [17592186341677 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341681 13194139535285 true] [17592186341677 1000 